issue.body:
**To reproduce:**

<!-- If the issue you reported requires a complex codebase to reproduce, please provide a replicable method such as a Github repository, Codesandbox link, Stackblitz link, or other relevant method for maintainers to investigate your feedback effectively. Thanks ! -->
```less
@compPrefix: ~'hi';
.@{compPrefix}{
 color:red;
 &:not(.@{compPrefix}-one, .@{compPrefix}-two){
  color:blue
 }
}
```

```less
@compPrefix: ~'hi';
.@{compPrefix}{
 color:red;
 &:not(&-one, &-two){
  color:blue
 }
}
```

**Current behavior:**

<!-- A clear and concise description of what the bug is -->
```
ParseError: Missing closing ')' in /Users/lar/work/isv/theme_static/test.less on line 4, column 26:
3  color:red;
4  &:not(.@{compPrefix}-one, .@{compPrefix}-two){
5   color:blue
```

**Expected behavior:**
Output like this;
```css
.hi {
  color: red;
}
.hi:not(.hi-one, .hi-two){
  color: blue;
}

```
<!-- A clear and concise description of what you expected to happen -->

**Environment information:**

<!-- Provide the `less` and `nodejs` packages versions -->

- `less` version: 4.1.2
- `nodejs` version: 16.14.0
- `operating system`: macos
<!-- macos, linux or windows ? -->

<!-- feel free to add additional comments -->

@jpattishall-ebay raised an issue in https://github.com/less/less.js/issues/4267#issuecomment-2552268095 where they noted ```@media``` and ```@container```  are not properly nesting in some cases.

Currently I see in 4.2.1 [Playground](https://lesscss.org/less-preview/#eyJjb2RlIjoiQG1lZGlhIG9ubHkgc2NyZWVuIGFuZCAobWluLXdpZHRoOiA3NjhweCkge1xuICBAY29udGFpbmVyIChtaW4td2lkdGg6IDUwMHB4KSB7XG4gICAgLnByaW1hcnktY29udGVudCB7XG4gICAgICBmb250LXNpemU6IDFyZW07XG4gICAgfVxuICB9XG59IiwiYWN0aXZlVmVyc2lvbiI6IjQuMi4xIiwibWF0aCI6InBhcmVucy1kaXZpc2lvbiIsInN0cmljdFVuaXRzIjpmYWxzZX0=) I see this:

```css
@media only screen and (min-width: 768px) {
  @container (min-width: 500px) {
    .primary-content {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
}
```

results in:

```css
@container only screen and (min-width: 768px) and (min-width: 500px) {
  .primary-content {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
}
```

But I see [4.1.3](https://lesscss.org/less-preview/#eyJjb2RlIjoiQG1lZGlhIG9ubHkgc2NyZWVuIGFuZCAobWluLXdpZHRoOiA3NjhweCkge1xuICBAY29udGFpbmVyIChtaW4td2lkdGg6IDUwMHB4KSB7XG4gICAgLnByaW1hcnktY29udGVudCB7XG4gICAgICBmb250LXNpemU6IDFyZW07XG4gICAgfVxuICB9XG59IiwiYWN0aXZlVmVyc2lvbiI6IjQuMS4zIiwibWF0aCI6InBhcmVucy1kaXZpc2lvbiIsInN0cmljdFVuaXRzIjpmYWxzZX0=) produced the expected output:

```css
@media only screen and (min-width: 768px) {
  @container (min-width: 500px) {
    .primary-content {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
}
```
